<diagram program="umlet" version="15.1">
  <help_text>Backend Architecture - FastAPI Application
Layer: Presentation (API/Web) → Core (Services) → Infrastructure (DB)</help_text>
  <zoom_level>8</zoom_level>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>96</x>
      <y>776</y>
      <w>320</w>
      <h>224</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>&lt;&lt;Infrastructure Layer&gt;&gt;
engine.py
--
Database connection and session management
--
+ engine: Engine
+ get_session() → Generator[Session]
+ session_scope() → Generator[Session]
+ wait_for_database(max_attempts, delay)
--
Dependencies:
- SQLModel/SQLAlchemy
- PostgreSQL or SQLite
--
Pattern: Factory + Context Manager
Creates DB sessions for dependency injection</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>456</x>
      <y>776</y>
      <w>320</w>
      <h>224</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>&lt;&lt;Infrastructure Layer&gt;&gt;
models.py
--
ORM table definitions (SQLModel)
--
+ Course(id, code, name, grading_scale)
+ Semester(id, name, year, course_id)
+ Subject(id, code, name, semester_id, ...)
+ Assignment(id, subject_id, assessment, ...)
+ Examination(id, subject_id, exam_mark, ...)
+ ExamSettings(id, subject_id, ps_exam, ...)
+ GradeScale(id, scale_name, grade, ...)
+ CourseSubjectLink(course_id, subject_id)
--
Pattern: Active Record (ORM)
Defines database schema and relationships</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>96</x>
      <y>456</y>
      <w>320</w>
      <h>240</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>&lt;&lt;Core Service Layer&gt;&gt;
CourseManager
--
Manages course business logic
--
- session: Session
--
+ create_course(name, code) → Course
+ get_all_courses() → list[Course]
+ get_course_by_id(id) → Course | None
+ get_course_by_code(code) → Course | None
+ add_subject_to_course(course_id, subject_id)
+ assign_semester_to_course(course_id, sem_id)
+ assign_year_to_course(course_id, year)
+ unassign_semester_from_course(...)
+ get_unassigned_semesters() → list[Semester]
+ update_course(id, name, code) → Course
+ delete_course(id) → bool
--
Pattern: Service Layer
Encapsulates course-related operations</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>456</x>
      <y>456</y>
      <w>320</w>
      <h>160</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>&lt;&lt;Core Service Layer&gt;&gt;
SubjectManager
--
Manages subject business logic
--
- session: Session
--
+ get_all_subjects() → list[Subject]
--
Pattern: Service Layer
Provides subject-related operations
(Currently minimal, extensible for future)</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>816</x>
      <y>456</y>
      <w>320</w>
      <h>200</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>&lt;&lt;Core Service Layer&gt;&gt;
SemesterManager
--
Manages semester business logic
--
- session: Session
--
+ get_all_semesters() → list[Semester]
+ get_distinct_years() → list[int]
+ get_semesters_for_course(course_id)
+ get_distinct_years_for_course(course_id)
--
Pattern: Service Layer
Handles semester queries and aggregations
Orders results (newest first)</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
  <element>
    <id>UMLClass</id>
    <coordinates>
      <x>1232</x>
      <y>456</y>
      <w>304</w>
      <h>240</h>
    </coordinates>
    <panel_attributes>&lt;&lt;Core Service Layer&gt;&gt;
GradeCalculator
--
Calculates academic metrics
--
- session: Session
--
+ calculate_wam(course_id) → float | None
+ calculate_gpa(course_id) → float | None
+ calculate_grade_counts(course_id) → dict[str, int]
- _get_grade_scales(course_id) → list[GradeScale]
--
Pattern: Service Layer + Strategy
Computes WAM (weighted average mark),
GPA (grade point average), and grade distributions
Uses GradeScale from DB for configurable grading
Auto-seeds default "Standard" scale if missing</panel_attributes>
    <additional_attributes/>
  </element>
